@using DYS.Molargo.Shared.Features.Inventory.ViewModels

@*
    The design's lab-case tracker. Work still out at the lab sorts first and soonest-due
    within that, because that is the order the fit appointments come up in.

    "Mark received" is the one action, and it closes a real loop: the diary's pre-booking
    check refuses a fit visit while the case is still out, so this is the screen that
    unblocks it.
*@

<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1.6fr_1fr]">
    <div class="border-divider px-6 py-5 lg:border-r-2">
        <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-3">
            <h5 class="m-0">Lab case tracking</h5>

            @if (Vm.OverdueLabCount > 0)
            {
                <span class="tag tag-accent">@Vm.OverdueLabCount overdue</span>
            }
        </div>

        @if (Vm.LabCases.Count == 0)
        {
            <p class="text-sm text-ink/55">
                No lab cases. A case is raised against a patient's planned crown, denture
                or appliance and tracked from here until it comes back.
            </p>
        }
        else
        {
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                <table class="w-full border-collapse">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th class="head-cell">Patient</th>
                            <th class="head-cell">Work</th>
                            <th class="head-cell">Lab</th>
                            <th class="head-cell">Sent</th>
                            <th class="head-cell">Due</th>
                            <th class="head-cell">Status</th>
                            <th class="head-cell"></th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        @foreach (var row in Vm.LabCases)
                        {
                            <tr>
                                <td class="body-cell">
                                    <button type="button"
                                            class="cursor-pointer border-0 bg-transparent p-0 text-left font-[inherit] font-bold text-ink hover:text-accent"
                                            @onclick="() => Vm.OpenPatientCommand.Execute(row.PatientId)">
                                        @row.PatientName
                                    </button>
                                </td>
                                <td class="body-cell text-xs">
                                    @row.Description

                                    @if (row.ToothNumber is { Length: > 0 } tooth)
                                    {
                                        @* Its own line rather than trailing the
                                           description: Razor trims the leading space out
                                           of an inline span, so "zirconia" and "46" ran
                                           together into a tooth number nobody has. *@
                                        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] text-ink/55">
                                            Tooth @tooth
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                </td>
                                <td class="body-cell text-xs">@(row.LabName ?? "—")</td>
                                <td class="body-cell text-xs">
                                    @(row.SentUtc is { } sent ? MolargoFormat.DayLabel(sent) : "—")
                                </td>
                                <td class="@InventoryCss.LabDueCell(row.IsOverdue(Vm.Today))">
                                    @(row.DueOn is { } due ? MolargoFormat.Date(due) : "—")

                                    @if (row.IsOverdue(Vm.Today))
                                    {
                                        <div class="text-[11px]">Overdue</div>
                                    }
                                </td>
                                <td class="body-cell">
                                    <span class="@InventoryCss.LabStatusTag(row.Status)">
                                        @InventoryCss.LabStatusLabel(row.Status)
                                    </span>
                                </td>
                                <td class="body-cell">
                                    @if (row.CanReceive)
                                    {
                                        <button class="btn btn-ghost whitespace-nowrap"
                                                disabled="@Vm.IsBusy"
                                                @onclick="() => Vm.ReceiveLabCaseCommand.ExecuteAsync(row.LabCaseId)">
                                            Mark received
                                        </button>
                                    }
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-ink/55">
                Booking a fit visit is refused while the case is still out — the diary's
                pre-booking check reads this list. <strong>Mark received</strong> is what
                clears it, so mark a case back when the box arrives rather than when it is
                fitted.
            </p>
        }
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 px-6 py-5">
        <h5 class="m-0">Lab prescription</h5>

        @*
            The design shows a filled prescription — shade A3 body, porcelain fused to
            zirconia, chamfer margin, scan and photo attachments — beside the list. None
            of that is on the lab case: it carries the patient, the work, the lab and the
            dates, and nothing else.

            Shown as what it needs rather than as sample values. A shade printed on screen
            that nobody chose is the kind of detail a technician would work to.
        *@
        <p class="text-sm text-ink/55">
            A lab prescription is the instruction sheet that travels with the case: shade,
            material, margin design, occlusal scheme, and the scans, bite records and
            photographs attached to it.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink/55">
            None of that is recorded yet — a case here holds the patient, the work, the
            lab and the dates. Writing prescriptions from Molargo also needs somewhere to
            put the attachments and a way to get them to the laboratory, which is online
            work.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-surface p-3 text-[13px]">
            <strong>What is tracked</strong>
            <div class="text-xs text-ink/70">
                Patient, work and tooth, laboratory, date sent, date due, and whether the
                case is back. That is enough to stop a fit visit being booked against work
                still at the lab, which is what the due-date check exists for.
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public InventoryViewModel Vm { get; set; } = default!;
}
